    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but the Bruen decision basically says if there isn't a historical precedent from the 1700s or 1800s, the law is unconstitutional. since most modern gun control is meant to address modern problems like mass shootings, doesn't that mean the \"historical analog\" argument is just a way to pretend modern safety needs don't matter? it feels like the legal door for actual regulation is basically slammed shut.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
